---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import DecisionPathBlock from "../../components/DecisionPathBlock.astro";
import EvidenceLimitsBlock from "../../components/EvidenceLimitsBlock.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import { editorialTeam } from "../../data/editorial";
import { cx30GuideQuality } from "../../data/mazda-cx30-quality";

const title = "2020 Mazda CX-30: what to check before buying";
const description = "A source-backed used-buyer inspection for the 2020 Mazda CX-30, covering VIN records, scheduled maintenance, brakes, tires, and front-suspension noise.";
const image = "/images/photos/cars/mazda-cx-30-2020.webp";
const modifiedTime = new Date("2026-09-01");
const quality = cx30GuideQuality["mazda-cx-30-2020-what-to-check-before-buying"];
const breadcrumbs = [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" }, { label: title }];
const related = [
  { href: "/problems/front-end-clunk-over-bumps-mazda-cx-30-2020/", title: "CX-30 front rattle over bumps", description: "Read the diagnostic steps when the viewing or road test reveals a repeatable front noise.", eyebrow: "Diagnosis" },
  { href: "/guides/mazda-cx-30-2020-service-schedule-and-maintenance-record/", title: "CX-30 service schedule and maintenance record", description: "Compare invoices with Mazda's maintenance context before agreeing a price.", eyebrow: "Maintenance" },
  { href: "/checklists/used-car-viewing/", title: "Printable used-car viewing worksheet", description: "Record documents, cold-start observations, road-test notes, and negotiations in one place.", eyebrow: "Worksheet" }
];
---

<ContentLayout title={title} description={description} intro="A clean-looking CX-30 still needs a VIN-led review of its records, recall status, tires, brakes, and road-test behavior. Treat a front rattle as a diagnosis task, not an automatic parts purchase." image={image} modifiedTime={modifiedTime} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} editorialSummary="A used-buyer inspection path tied to Mazda's service material, a published recall report, and the specific front-suspension scope already documented for this model." editorialByline={`By ${editorialTeam.name}`} editorialReviewedLabel="Reviewed September 1, 2026" editorialBadges={["Used-buyer guide", "US-market scope", "Source-backed"]}>
  <EvidenceLimitsBlock {...quality.evidence} />
  <DecisionPathBlock title="Start with records and condition" intro="Use documents, VIN information, and the observed vehicle before treating the model name as evidence of condition." steps={quality.decisionPath} />

  <Section title="Before arranging a viewing" intro="Ask for enough information to decide whether the trip and a pre-purchase inspection are worthwhile.">
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Request the VIN, mileage, trim, drivetrain, title status, maintenance invoices, and details of any prior suspension or brake repair.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Check open recalls by VIN. The published brake-caliper recall report describes a defined 2020 production population; it cannot confirm completion on one vehicle.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Compare service records with Mazda's <a class="font-semibold text-accent hover:underline" href="https://www.mazdausa.com/static/manuals/2020/cx-30/contents/07020601.html" rel="noopener" target="_blank">scheduled-maintenance guidance</a>. Missing records justify a baseline service budget, not a remote diagnosis.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Cold inspection and walk-around" intro="See the vehicle before a short drive or a seller explanation turns the inspection into a general impression.">
    <p>Check paint, panel alignment, glass, lamps, underbody marks, fluid traces, tire date codes, tread pattern, and whether all four tires match in size and type. Uneven tire wear can support an alignment, suspension, or impact question, but it does not identify the cause by itself. Record the tire condition beside the asking price because a full set can materially change the first-year budget.</p>
    <p class="mt-4">Start the vehicle cold where possible. Watch the warning lamps, idle behavior, climate control, cameras, windows, locks, and infotainment. For safety systems, abnormal warning lights, braking changes, steering looseness, or visible wheel movement are reasons to pause the purchase and obtain a professional inspection.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Road-test checks" intro="Use a route that includes low speed, turns, uneven pavement, and a safe faster section when conditions allow.">
    <p>Listen for a front rattle over bumps and note the road surface, speed, steering angle, braking input, and whether the noise remains after the vehicle warms up. Mazda's published front-suspension material has defined build and symptom conditions; a similar noise can also involve mounts, dampers, brake hardware, or other suspension components. Do not use a short rattle as proof that the car needs links.</p>
    <p class="mt-4">At normal road speed, observe steering pull, vibration, braking response, and tire noise. Begin the follow-up with tire condition, pressure, balance, and alignment history before pricing suspension or bearing work. A clean road test does not replace a workshop inspection, but it gives the workshop useful conditions to reproduce.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Decide what changes the price" intro="Separate a manageable baseline from evidence that makes the purchase too uncertain.">
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><p class="eyebrow">Reasonable baseline</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Documented routine service, normal brakes and tires, VIN recall confirmation, and a road test without unresolved safety symptoms. Budget only for confirmed near-term maintenance.</p></article>
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><p class="eyebrow">Pause or walk away</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">No VIN or service history, contradictory mileage or repair story, warning lamps, braking or steering changes, or a seller unwilling to allow an independent inspection.</p></article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <RelatedLinks title="CX-30 next steps" intro="Move from the viewing evidence to the relevant record or diagnosis." items={related} />
</ContentLayout>
